### success with an explicit -author (stub answers: token)
$ env GRAIN_TOKEN=BEFD-5JHV-6FP4-34MX-SQ3Z-QJAF-LJMF-7LP4 timeout 60 /home/debian/bin/grain --server http://127.0.0.1:4291 git-login -web -host 127.0.0.1:4297 -base-url http://127.0.0.1:4297 -scope acme/widgets -author Dana Example
    ! First copy your one-time code: WDJB-MJHT
    - Open http://127.0.0.1:4297/login/device in your browser to authorize Grain...
      (Could not open browser automatically: exec: "xdg-open,x-www-browser,www-browser": executable file not found in $PATH)
    Authenticated to 127.0.0.1:4297 as Dana Example: this deployment now clones, pushes, and signs new pull requests and comments as "Signed by Dana Example (via Grain)".
    -> exit=0
    poll: {"answer":"token","gap_s":null,"grant_type_ok":true}
== what the deployment stored (token never echoed)
### deployment git connections
$ sh -c env GRAIN_TOKEN=BEFD-5JHV-6FP4-34MX-SQ3Z-QJAF-LJMF-7LP4 /home/debian/bin/grain --server http://127.0.0.1:4291 -json deployment 2>/dev/null | jq -c '.gitConnections // .git // empty' | head -c 2000
    -> exit=0
    ok: the delegated token is not readable back
